
# Generated at build time from hardware/cad by scripts/build-shop-catalogue.ts.
# Deliberately NOT committed: a copy of cad's designs in this lane's git would
# be a second source of truth and would drift silently. See that file's header.
public/shop/
public/shop.building-*/
.shop-building-*/
public/shop.old-*/

# The external design shelf: metadata about OTHER PEOPLE'S openly-licensed
# designs, plus a scratch cache of sources fetched to test them.
# Deliberately NOT committed, for two reasons that are not the same:
#   1. like public/shop/, a checked-in index of someone else's tree drifts;
#   2. the fetched sources are third-party work under their own licences, and
#      committing them would republish them from our repository — which is the
#      one thing this pipeline is built not to do.
# SEPARATE from public/shop/ because build-shop-catalogue.ts wipes its own
# output directory, and a shared one silently deleted this shelf.
public/designs/

# Third-party design sources fetched to TEST them. Deliberately OUTSIDE public/:
# Vite copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, so a cache under it would be SERVED
# from our origin — republishing other people's work as a side effect of a
# directory choice, and invisibly, because the cards link out.
.design-src/

# The PnP 3D view's board render, generated from pcb's gerbers by
# scripts/build-pnp-stackup.ts. Not committed for the same reason as public/shop/:
# a rendered copy of another lane's fab files drifts the day they re-export.
public/pnp-stackup/
public/pnp-stackup.building-*/

# The pcb tab's gate records, collected from pcb's tree by
# scripts/build-pcb-gates.ts. Not committed: a copy of another lane's gate
# results drifts the moment pcb re-runs a gate.
public/pcb-gates/
